---
// Every claim on this page was checked against the code rather than written
// from a template: the field lists come from the three form definitions in
// [county]/index.astro, the analytics description from lib/gtag.ts, and the
// listing_events description from lib/analytics.ts, which writes three
// columns and no identifier of any kind.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const UPDATED = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Verified Home Inspector"
  description="What Verified Home Inspector collects, what it does with it, and who it is shared with. Homeowner requests go to one inspector and are never sold or resold."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

        <p>
          Verified Home Inspector is operated by Sunstate Bay Ventures LLC, a Florida limited
          liability company. This page describes what the site collects, what happens to it, and
          who it goes to. It is written to be read rather than to be comprehensive, so if
          something here is unclear, ask and we will answer it plainly.
        </p>

        <h2>The directory itself is public record</h2>
        <p>
          The inspector names, license numbers, cities, and license statuses in this directory
          come from the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation, which
          publishes them as public records. We did not collect them from the inspectors listed,
          and an inspector does not have to give us anything to appear here. The DBPR extract
          carries no phone numbers and no email addresses, so neither appears on a listing
          unless the inspector gave it to us themselves.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are listed and believe your record is wrong, tell us and we will correct it
          against the current DBPR record.
        </p>

        <h2>What you send us through a form</h2>
        <p>There are three forms on this site, and each collects only what it needs.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Requesting an inspector.</strong> Your name, email address, phone number if
            you give one, the city or ZIP of the property, the kind of inspection you want, and
            anything you write in the message box. The county and the name and license number of
            the inspector you chose are recorded with it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Claiming a listing.</strong> Your license number, your name, your business
            name if you give one, your email address, your phone number if you give one, and
            which plan you selected.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Asking about a featured spot.</strong> The same details as a claim, plus
            anything you write in the message box.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each form also contains a hidden field that a person never sees. Automated submissions
          fill it in and real people do not, so anything that arrives with it filled is
          discarded as spam.
        </p>

        <h2>Where a homeowner request goes</h2>
        <p>
          A request goes to the one inspector you selected, and to nobody else. We do not send
          the same homeowner to several inspectors, we do not sell contact details, and we do not
          charge inspectors for individual leads. We keep a count of how many requests a listing
          has received, because a listing is free until it has received five and that count is
          how the billing promise is kept.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and to count how many times the
          request, claim, and featured buttons are used. Google Analytics sets cookies in your
          browser and collects the usual technical information: pages viewed, approximate
          location derived from your IP address, and your device and browser type. It runs only
          on the live site, so visits to development and preview versions are not recorded.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can prevent this by blocking cookies in your browser settings, or by installing the
          Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on that Google publishes.
        </p>

        <h2>Counting clicks on a listing</h2>
        <p>
          When a request button is used, the site records three things in its own database: which
          listing was clicked, what kind of click it was, and which part of the page it came
          from. It does not record your name, your email address, your IP address, or any
          identifier that could be traced back to you, and there is no way to reconstruct who
          clicked from what is stored. These rows exist so an inspector can be shown how much
          interest their listing has drawn.
        </p>

        <h2>Companies that process this on our behalf</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts the site and receives the form submissions.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> provides the visit and button counts described above.</li>
          <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores the directory and the click counts.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each of these has its own privacy policy governing what it does with what it handles.
        </p>

        <h2>How long any of it is kept</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are kept while they are useful — a homeowner request until the
          inspection is arranged and long enough after that to resolve any question about it, and
          an inspector's claim for as long as the listing is active. Ask us to delete a
          submission and we will, unless we are required to keep it.
        </p>

        <h2>Asking what we hold, or asking us to delete it</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be
          deleted. Use the form on the directory page and we will reply to the address you give
          us. We may need to confirm you are who you say you are before acting on a request about
          someone else's details.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is meant for adults arranging or performing home inspections. It is not
          directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect anything from them.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it. Material
          changes will be described on the page rather than folded in silently.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy go through the same forms as everything else. Use the
          <a href="/fl/pinellas/#claim">form on the directory page</a> and we will reply to the
          address you give us.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
